####################################################################
# cat1b_withdraw.rq — CAT1b withdrawal condition. HAND-AUTHORED.
#
# A CAT1b flag ("asystole while an arterial line is present without alarms
# on its pathway") is withdrawn when an alarm on that same IBP pathway
# arrives while the flagged asystole is still active (agreed 2026-09-21):
# in a genuine asystole the pressure alarm naturally follows the ECG alarm
# by seconds, so the flag set at onset must not stand. The withdrawn
# asystole becomes evidence for a clinical event from this moment on.
#
# A CAT1a flag rests on a signal or sensor, never on a functional unit, so a
# withdrawal never touches it. A stored flag lives in the flagged alarm's
# own transient graph, so only flags of alarms still active are found.
#
# CONTRACT. Bound on entry: ?new (the arriving alarm, on an IBP functional
# unit). Binds: ?flagged (the flagged alarm), ?fu, ?gFlag (the graph
# holding the flag).
# Used by actions/flag_withdraw_select.rq (logged as cat1b_withdrawn) and
# actions/flag_withdraw_delete.rq.
#
# VALIDATION — engine/regression.py: cat1b_withdraw and cat3a_withdraw
# (withdrawn), cat1b_borrow (forbidden firing: no withdrawal of the
# asystole there).
####################################################################

PREFIX mda:    <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX mdapoc: <https://w3id.org/mda/poc#>

GRAPH ?gNew { ?new mda:hasMessage ?newMsg . ?newMsg mda:triggeredBy ?fu . }
GRAPH ?gFlag { ?flagged mdapoc:flaggedLikelyFalsePositive ?fu }
